---
import "../styles/global.css";

const description =
  "Web developer from Dhaka, Bangladesh, building for the web and open source. Find my GitHub and email address here, and the story behind the domain name.";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "https://rxvn.cc/#website",
      url: "https://rxvn.cc/",
      name: "rxvn",
      alternateName: "Reshad Ahammed Ayon",
    },
    {
      "@type": "ProfilePage",
      url: "https://rxvn.cc/",
      mainEntity: {
        "@type": "Person",
        "@id": "https://rxvn.cc/#person",
        name: "Reshad Ahammed Ayon",
        alternateName: ["rxvn", "rxvncc"],
        url: "https://rxvn.cc/",
        description: "Web developer from Dhaka, Bangladesh.",
        jobTitle: "Web Developer",
        address: {
          "@type": "PostalAddress",
          addressLocality: "Dhaka",
          addressCountry: "BD",
        },
        knowsAbout: [
          "Free and Open Source Software",
          "Full-Stack Development",
          "Software Development",
          "Web Development",
        ],
        sameAs: ["https://github.com/rxvncc"],
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>rxvn.cc</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://rxvn.cc/" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="profile" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="rxvn" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Reshad Ahammed Ayon (rxvn)" />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://rxvn.cc/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://rxvn.cc/og.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta
      property="og:image:alt"
      content="Reshad Ahammed Ayon, Web Developer, rxvn.cc"
    />
    <meta property="profile:first_name" content="Reshad" />
    <meta property="profile:last_name" content="Ahammed Ayon" />
    <meta property="profile:username" content="rxvncc" />

    <!-- Twitter / X (falls back to the Open Graph tags above) -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />

    <!-- Icons -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />

    <!-- Structured data -->
    <script
      is:inline
      type="application/ld+json"
      set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}
    />
  </head>
  <body class="p-6 font-mono bg-white text-black dark:bg-black dark:text-white">
    <header>
      <p>My name is Reshad Ahammed Ayon, but you can call me Ayon.</p>
      <p>I develop websites from Dhaka, Bangladesh.</p>
    </header>
    <main class="max-w-prose mt-4 space-y-4">
      <p>
        If you're wondering about rxvn.cc, the first part, rxvn, is a numeronym,
        similar to i18n. It's made up of the first and last letters of my name,
        with the 15 letters in between represented by XV (the Roman numeral for
        15). As for .cc, I chose it because it was short and affordable compared
        to the alternatives. Together, the entire domain is just seven
        characters long.
      </p>
      <p>
        I try to use rxvncc as my username across third-party platforms. It's
        simply this domain without the dot. Since rxvn is sometimes already
        taken, and some platforms don't allow periods in usernames, rxvncc makes
        for a convenient alternative.
      </p>
      <p>
        I don't currently maintain a blog or an active social media presence. I
        used to, but eventually came to the conclusion that these platforms
        aren't as beneficial as they might seem. Of course, they can be useful,
        or even necessary, for some people. Fortunately, I haven't found myself
        needing them so far.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm not particularly active on instant messaging platforms. Email is my
        preferred way to communicate.
      </p>
    </main>
    <footer class="mt-4 gap-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row">
      <a href="mailto:contact@rxvn.cc" class="underline">
        contact@rxvn.cc
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/rxvncc" rel="me" class="underline">
        github.com/rxvncc
      </a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
